{"reference":"Isaiah 18","book":"Isaiah","chapter":18,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Wider Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One disputed reading of Isaiah’s wider pattern sees the book addressing Judah, Israel, and foreign nations together: empires can serve a role in the story yet remain answerable themselves, while nations can also be pictured as learning, worshiping, and sharing in restoration. That larger pattern provides a useful frame for a chapter that moves from a distant people to a gift brought to Mount Zion.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_018_9a90acfd6164cba145b20a66"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}